    "reason": "The only evidence is a one-line changelog title [ev-d83aa8e2cc23]. It says log RBAC is now enforced by default. It does not name the setting that controls enforcement, its old default, or which RBAC policies or roles lose log access. Whether a user is exposed depends on their configured RBAC policy and that enforcement setting, not on runtime behaviour. So the proposed runtime-behavior-gap undecidable leaf mislabels this, but the evidence is too thin to write the correct predicate. To decide, we need the upgrade-guide text naming the enforcement setting and the policy.csv permission that grants log access.",
